<title>FRANCE: GAN makes 281 mln Ffr on Belgian sale.</title>
<headline>GAN makes 281 mln Ffr on Belgian sale.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>French state-owned insurer Groupe des Assurances Nationales (GAN) will make a capital gain of 281 million French francs on the sale of GAN Belgium to Swiss Life Belgium, a GAN spokesman told Reuters.  </p>
<p>The gain represents 49 percent of the sale price of 575 million francs.</p>
<p>GAN Belgium had a turnover of 3.4 billion Belgian francs in 1995, of which 59 percent came from non-life insurance, and reported a profit of 219 million Belgian francs, versus 36 million Belgian francs a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
